# .sgl/immutable-paths — paths agents and loops may READ but never MODIFY.
# Owned by the Human Steward. Changes to this file are human-approved governance events.
# One entry per line. A trailing "/" protects a whole directory. Globs (*, ?) are allowed.
# A line starting with "!" is an exception (an allowed path inside a protected one).
# This file always protects itself; it cannot be excepted.

# Verifiers and evaluation harness
verifiers/
eval/

# Golden fixtures and baselines
tests/golden/
tests/fixtures/baselines/

# Scoring rubric for auto-research
auto-research/*/rubric.md

# The harness itself: rules, hooks, enforcement, and CI. Agents may read these;
# changing them is a Human Steward-approved change (R3).
# The handoff file is excepted because the Stop hook writes it every session.
.kiro/steering/
!.kiro/steering/next-session-prompt.md
.kiro/hooks/
.sgl/
.github/workflows/
CODEOWNERS
.github/CODEOWNERS

# SGL templates, if you vendor them into the repo
templates/B-TEAM-REVIEW-PACKAGE.md
templates/CODE-REVIEW-PROMPT-*
templates/GATE-EVIDENCE-CHECKLIST.md
templates/HOOKS-SESSION-STATE.md
templates/INTENT-CONTRACT.md
templates/enforcement/
